    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling matchups against soft opposing rotations. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.14) anchors our daily outlook, benefiting from a highly favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Law that pushes his efficiency score well into the strong tier. Similarly, **Trevor Story** (67.25) presents a premium play; facing the hittable Rodriguez, he leverages a significant park factor boost and SP skill matchup to solidify his spot as an essential contributor. While **Seiya Suzuki** (62.04) and **Griffin Conine** (60.12) both hover in the strong category, **Griffin Conine** is particularly compelling today, as his favorable matchup against Tong\u2014who carries a generous 5.63 xERA\u2014provides the highest situational upside of our outfielders.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board was excluding **Zach McKinstry** (39.94) from the starting nine. Despite a respectable park factor, he fell just fractionally below our 40.0 efficiency floor, largely neutralized by the difficulty of facing Ryan. Elsewhere, we are navigating inherent volatility: both **Max Muncy** and **James Wood** face elite pitching in Cease and Pivetta respectively, which suppresses their scores significantly despite their natural talent. Furthermore, **Brice Turang** remains a primary objective for our stolen base pursuit, though his score is tempered by a tough matchup against Boyd and the defensive efficiency of the opposing battery. We will continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Edwin Arroyo**, whose sub-floor projection makes him a potential liability if he drifts further down the batting order before first pitch.",
